        "You can read it. It is a calendar of the sun on the pans, cut in the oak by the first pan-keeper, in a script that is half marks and half arithmetic. The Gaos get the noon and the dawn of the long days, the Tans the dawn and dusk of the short. Neither family has had the whole of anything. The board is fair.",
        "You carve a new board from the old marks with a borrowed knife. It takes a night. In the morning both families come to the channel. Xiao Er stands between them, holding the new board up in both hands like a tray. The sun is just up, and the brine runs gold. Nobody speaks.",
